.TH FINANCE-MAIL-INGEST 1 "2026-11-12" "Finance Infrastructure" "Nexus Host Utilities"
.SH NAME
finance-mail-ingest \- stage authenticated bank alerts and candidate validated-receipt links
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /opt/data/bin/finance-mail-ingest
.RB [ --preview | --apply ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses the existing Nexus localhost Proton Bridge IMAP connection and Bitwarden
Secrets Manager credential to inspect CIBC purchase-alert emails without changing
mail flags. Only the exact supported sender/subject/body template with aligned
CIBC DKIM is parsed. Other subjects are ignored; unexpected template or
security failures block an apply run. The mail header date is only an alert
receipt time, not proof of the purchase or bank-posting date.
.PP
The default
.B --preview
is read-only. With
.B --apply
it extends the
.B transaction_email_alerts
table in the existing finance-analytics PostgreSQL database, stores parsed
amount/merchant/provenance, and updates tentative one-to-one links against
.B validated, nonduplicate CAD receipts
from both Metro email and scanned Receipt Wrangler sources. Exact CAD cents,
near-date and strong merchant are required; ambiguity is held for review.
The new
.B purchase_receipt_id
references the validated analytics receipt. For scanned receipts only, the
existing Wrangler ID is also retained. The
.B v_purchase_item_tracking
view exposes every validated item observation with observed unit price and
separate email/bank candidate states; receipt line items remain traceable
without inventing a bank expense or treating a candidate as confirmed.
Message-ID hashes prevent duplicate ingestion on UID/UIDVALIDITY changes. No
raw email body, card suffix or credentials are persisted. Existing Receipt
Wrangler and Wealthfolio transactions are never created or modified.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Host Python 3.9+, Docker/psql, systemd-creds, bws, the existing local Proton
Bridge IMAP listener on 127.0.0.1:1143, projected validated receipts and
finance-analytics PostgreSQL, and root-only
.B /etc/nexus/secrets/finance-imap-user
(mode 0600). Confirm a current protected and tested finance-analytics backup
before applying a schema change. The receipt projection runs first in
.B finance-intake.service
so newly uploaded scanned items are available for the email match in the same
hourly cycle.
.SH OUTPUT
Aggregate counts and generic errors only. Exit 0 means preview or apply/readback
completed; nonzero means stop and review. No automatic timer is installed by
this executable.
.SH ROLLBACK
Inspect the exact source-key/receipt links and any later consumers. Remove
only reviewed candidate references or restore the previous view definition;
never roll the complete live database back over later receipts or owner writes. The
private
.B iragonforce/ops
repository owns the script and this manual.
